{"kind":"artifact","text":"The architecture reference, unchanged at this head and republished so the artifact set stands at one exact commit. Exact clean pushed head 6bcb4798e07efe3a8c8de4a495e709520cf099e7 on request/planner-dr-recut; checkout clean, local and origin identical. Successor to ec935b30 at this path.\n\nNOTHING IN THIS PAGE CHANGED, AND I WANT TO BE EXPLICIT ABOUT WHY THAT IS A JUDGEMENT RATHER THAN AN OMISSION. My two commits add signingRefusal at two browser signing sites and correct comments in a test. Neither changes a layer contract: the browser still derives nothing the fold does not project, the predicates it consults are the ones layer 5 already publishes, and no projection field, schema or profile moved. The @13-to-@14 advance this page records is 97a749ec's and is untouched.\n\nSo the page is accurate as it stands, and editing it to mention the new dispatcher would be documenting an implementation detail of layer 7 in a page about contracts between layers. The passage that matters to this head is already there and was written before it: that a departed actor may still supersede an earlier act they authored, and that the narrow cleanup exception confers no force on a new state or a ratification. That sentence is what makes the supersede branch of signingRefusal an exemption rather than an oversight.\n\nIF THE REVIEWER DISAGREES, that is a legitimate call to make against me rather than a misunderstanding to correct. codex blocked an earlier head in this family precisely because its prose claimed a coverage the code did not have, and the mirror-image error — code acquiring a behaviour the page does not describe — is the one I could be making here. I have argued it is not a contract change; if you judge that the layer 5 to layer 7 derivation boundary now needs to say where authority is asked, request changes and I will write it rather than defend the omission.\n\nThe three profile numbers on the page remain three different historical facts: @14 for this lane's projection change, @13 for main's guarded unclaimed-reassignment bump, @12 for the older change. I re-checked that none of them needs renumbering, because the temptation on a republish is to tidy them into agreement and that would make the page describe a history that did not happen.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD: go test ./... -count=1 exit 0 with 34 ok and zero cached, which matters because the docset gate caches past documentation edits; gofmt clean; build and vet exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"6bcb4798e07efe3a8c8de4a495e709520cf099e7","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}